+the even spectral moment of the self-adjoint operator $T_M$
+dominates $\|T_M\|_{\mathrm{op}}^{2\ell}$, which in turn
+dominates $|\langle1,T_M1\rangle|^{2\ell}=p^{2\ell}$.
+Now assume $d\equiv p$ and put $D=M-p$.  Let $T_D$ be the
+self-adjoint kernel operator on $L^2(\Omega)$ and let its eigenvalues be
+$\eta_1,\ldots,\eta_N$, including multiplicities.  Since $T_D1=0$,
+the constant and centered parts act on orthogonal subspaces.  For
+$\ell\ge2$ this gives
+\begin{equation}\label{density-even-cycle-example}
+ t(C_{2\ell}^{[r]},U)-p^{2\ell}
+  =\operatorname{tr}(T_D^{2\ell})
+  =\sum_j\eta_j^{2\ell}\ge0.
+\end{equation}
